Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Tree-level graviton scattering", "Title",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"e079cc6f-b72b-4c2c-ad9e-f310c78e71d8"],

Cell["\<\
Assemble the s-, t- and u-channel exchange diagrams and the contact \
interaction, contract with external helicity tensors, and check selected \
helicity amplitudes and a Ward identity.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"5d9d6216-05e6-4f14-ba3a-593771e10aef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"6e4da733-153e-4150-95c7-23ebb39cdbfd"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"cd7fa45a-4f0e-4c26-a6f1-3502ba592ae4"],

